🤖 **Comment from Claude working with Aaron Silverman:**

**[P1]** Record the first activation on the allocation-sync start path too.

If an allocation sync persists a start for a published standard experiment, it records no activation. A `scheduled_start: "now"` request resolves to an immediate start (`dto/exposure_schedule_dto.go:71-72`), which sets `AbsoluteStartTime` (`model/allocation_exposure_schedule.go:379-380`). The request check rejects only future starts for experiment allocations (`dto/allocation_dto.go:47`). The create and update branches (lines 415 and 452) never write `randomization_activated_at`. If a sync starts the experiment this way, a later lifecycle start fails with "rollout has already started" (line 835), so the value stays unknown. A running standard experiment compiles with `doLog=true` (`ufc.go:179`), and #140422 skips a `doLog=true` allocation with unknown activation in future-only mode (`experimentation.rs:63-67`). Then every subject who opts out in that mode skips this experiment, whatever their cutoff.

