- I ran 38 inputs through chrono `DateTime::parse_from_rfc3339`, and through the `parseCutoff` below as a standalone program. All 38 agree on accept or reject. The 36 inputs without a leap second also agree on the instant.
- The 2 leap-second inputs map to the start of the next second. chrono orders a leap second after second 59 and before the next second, so the strict-before check gives the same result for every activation without a leap second.
- The test below fails at `7a1f3c52` on `2026-10-01t12:00:00z`. With the patch, `//domains/ffe/libs/flagging/ufc:go_default_test` passes.
